##### Runnable: interface with single method run() - java1.0
--------------------------
java.lang.Runnable: java.lang package, functional interface
  No return
  Cannot throw checked exception
  Used with Thread

public interface Runnable {
    void run();
}

Runnable r = () -> {
    System.out.println("Task running");
};

new Thread(r).start();
new Thread(() -> {
    System.out.println("Task running");
}).run();


#### Callable: interface with single method call() - java1.5
--------------------------
java.util.concurrent.Callable: java.util.concurrent package, functional interface
  Returns value
  Can throw exception
  Used with ExecutorService

public interface Callable<V> {
    V call() throws Exception;
}
Callable<Integer> c = () -> {
    return 42;
};

### start():
-------
  Creates new thread and calls run() internally in that thread
  Executes concurrently

### run():
------
  Normal method
  No new thread


| Method          | Description                 |
| --------------- | --------------------------- |
| `start()`       | Starts the thread           |
| `run()`         | Contains code to execute    |
| `sleep(ms)`     | Pauses thread               |
| `join()`        | Waits for thread to finish  |
| `isAlive()`     | Checks if thread is running |
| `setPriority()` | Sets thread priority        |
